    "lawCode": "Add Art 7 Title 18 §1600-t, amd §1600-b, rpld Art 7 Title 18, Pub Auth L",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S6993\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the public authorities law, in\nrelation to the village of Suffern parking authority and repealing\ntitle 18 of article 7 of such law relating thereto\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nTo abolish the Village of Suffern parking authority.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Adds a new section 1600-t to title 18 of article 7 of the\npublic authorities law (Village of Suffern Parking Authority) to\nprovide for the termination of the authority by December 31, 2014.\n\nSection 2. Amends section 1600-b of the public authorities law to\nprovide that the board and corporate existence of the Village of\nSuffern Parking Authority shall continue only to December 31, 2014.\n\nSection 3. Repeals title 18 of article 7 of the public authorities\nlaw.\n\nSection 4. Effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Suffern Parking Authority was created in 1974 at the request of\nthe Board of Trustees of the Village of Suffern. Since its inception,\nthe Authority has never incurred any bonded indebtedness and there is\nno bonded indebtedness currently outstanding. Since the functions\nperformed by the parking authority do, in certain respects, overlap\nwith those performed by the Village of Suffern, the Board of Trustees\ndesires to abolish the parking authority. Pursuant to the applicable\nauthorizing legislation, the parking authority's corporate existence\nis currently set to expire on December 31, 2019.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\nLOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect on December thirty-first, two thousand\nfourteen, except that section one of this act shall take effect on the\nthirtieth day after it shall have become a law.\n\n",
